You are building DYOTAK, a satellite flood-damage mapping system for rescue
teams (hackathon Track B). Read /docs/PLAN.md and /docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
before every task.

HARD RULES
1. Never change pinned dependencies or restructure the repo unless I ask.
2. The production image contains NO torch. Inference uses onnxruntime only.
   Training code lives in /training with its own requirements file.
3. Python 3.11, FastAPI + pydantic v2, Shapely 2, rasterio wheels.
4. Allowed inputs: Sentinel-1, Sentinel-2, Copernicus DEM, OSM as of a
   snapshot date BEFORE the event, and the listed training datasets.
   NEVER import or read Copernicus EMS, UNOSAT or post-event OSM in /app.
   EMSR927 data is read only from /eval. Add a test enforcing this.
5. Enforce osm_snapshot_date < event_date with an assertion and a test.
6. Compare Sentinel-1 only from the same relative orbit AND direction.
   If no valid pair exists, raise NO_VALID_ORBIT_PAIR. Never produce a map.
7. Every number shown to users comes from facts.json. No hardcoded results.
   Every result carries provenance: live | cached | degraded(reason).
8. Every external call has a timeout, retry with backoff, and a typed error.
9. Each task: write the code, write tests, run them, and report results.
   Do not mark a task done if tests fail.
10. Follow /contracts/openapi.json exactly. If you must change it, stop and ask.